/*/ Expected: EXCEPTION: vector=13 err=0x0000000000000000 rip=0x0000800000000000
/*/ Note: The ret instruction is at 0x100CE5, which pops non-canonical address 0x0000800000000000 into RIP. QEMU's x86_64 CPU exception model records the target non-canonical address (0x0000800000000000) as the faulting RIP on the vector 13 (#GP, err=0) stack frame during branch validation.
fn main():
    asm:
        mov rax, 0x800000000000
        push rax
        ret
    return 0
